  "evaluation": "B is best: it correctly identifies a genuine disagreement and selects the marked population difference as the clearest explanation, while noting design and outcome-measure differences. C is nearly equivalent and adds useful detail about self-reported deficiency versus measured serum levels. A also correctly calls the disagreement genuine, and its design-based explanation is defensible, but it less convincingly prioritizes design over population and labels exposure ascertainment as an intervention difference despite neither study administering vitamin D.",
  "ranking": ["B", "C", "A"]
}
